WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.582
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level four.

2
00:00:05.882 --> 00:00:09.524
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.824 --> 00:00:16.180
Unit nineteen: Future of Global Governance. Today you will evaluate reforms with the extent / degree to which.

4
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.005
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.967 --> 00:00:23.200
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:25.910
International institution.

7
00:00:26.917 --> 00:00:33.096
International institution means a permanent organisation created by several countries to work together.

8
00:00:33.683 --> 00:00:36.879
Each international institution has its own rules.

9
00:00:37.483 --> 00:00:40.960
Your turn. Say: International institution.

10
00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:45.683
International institution.

11
00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:47.834
Multilateralism.

12
00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:53.706
Multilateralism means the practice of countries solving problems together through shared rules.

13
00:00:54.317 --> 00:00:57.233
Multilateralism helped to end the crisis.

14
00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:01.118
Your turn. Say: Multilateralism.

15
00:01:03.967 --> 00:01:05.479
Multilateralism.

16
00:01:06.217 --> 00:01:07.810
Global cooperation.

17
00:01:08.817 --> 00:01:13.370
Global cooperation means nations working together to deal with worldwide problems.

18
00:01:13.983 --> 00:01:16.970
Global cooperation reduced the spread of disease.

19
00:01:17.583 --> 00:01:20.677
Your turn. Say: Global cooperation.

20
00:01:23.533 --> 00:01:25.219
Global cooperation.

21
00:01:25.983 --> 00:01:27.344
Reform proposal.

22
00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:32.962
Reform proposal means a suggested plan to change how an organisation works.

23
00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:36.444
The reform proposal would enlarge the council.

24
00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:40.144
Your turn. Say: Reform proposal.

25
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.535
Reform proposal.

26
00:01:45.283 --> 00:01:46.505
Emerging power.

27
00:01:47.517 --> 00:01:52.372
Emerging power means a country whose economic and political influence is growing fast.

28
00:01:52.983 --> 00:01:55.830
Every emerging power wants a stronger voice.

29
00:01:56.417 --> 00:01:59.475
Your turn. Say: Emerging power.

30
00:02:02.333 --> 00:02:03.671
Emerging power.

31
00:02:04.417 --> 00:02:05.708
Global challenge.

32
00:02:06.717 --> 00:02:11.038
Global challenge means a serious problem that affects many countries at once.

33
00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:13.847
Climate change is a global challenge.

34
00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:17.288
Your turn. Say: Global challenge.

35
00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:21.564
Global challenge.

36
00:02:22.317 --> 00:02:24.154
Institutional legitimacy.

37
00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:30.656
Institutional legitimacy means the public belief that an institution has the right to make decisions.

38
00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:34.596
Institutional legitimacy depends on fair procedures.

39
00:02:35.183 --> 00:02:38.997
Your turn. Say: Institutional legitimacy.

40
00:02:41.833 --> 00:02:43.717
Institutional legitimacy.

41
00:02:44.483 --> 00:02:45.717
Collective action.

42
00:02:46.717 --> 00:02:50.910
Collective action means people or states acting together to reach a shared goal.

43
00:02:51.517 --> 00:02:53.865
Collective action protected the ozone layer.

44
00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:57.497
Your turn. Say: Collective action.

45
00:03:00.333 --> 00:03:01.787
Collective action.

46
00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:06.390
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:13.629
Visal, a scholar writes 'The extent to which institutions reflect today's world is debatable.' What is 'the extent to which'?

48
00:03:14.717 --> 00:03:26.889
It is a formal noun phrase meaning 'how far'. 'The extent to which' and 'the degree to which' introduce a clause that is the subject: The degree to which power is shared affects legitimacy.

49
00:03:27.983 --> 00:03:29.553
Why is 'to' before 'which'?

50
00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:43.159
The clause comes from 'institutions reflect the world to some extent'. In formal English the preposition moves in front of 'which': the extent to which, the way in which, the reason for which.

51
00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:45.983
Can I use it in questions?

52
00:03:47.083 --> 00:03:58.408
Yes, in essays: 'To what extent should emerging powers have more influence?' It invites balanced evaluation, which is useful for discussing reform proposals.

53
00:03:59.567 --> 00:04:01.195
Part three: grammar.

54
00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:05.988
Grammar focus: The extent and degree to which plus clause.

55
00:04:06.288 --> 00:04:07.510
Look at the pattern.

56
00:04:08.217 --> 00:04:12.167
The extent to which institutions reflect today's world is widely debated.

57
00:04:13.083 --> 00:04:17.498
The degree to which emerging powers are heard affects institutional legitimacy.

58
00:04:18.383 --> 00:04:21.741
The way in which decisions are made determines public trust.

59
00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:31.436
Use the extent / degree to which + clause as a formal subject meaning 'how far'. The preposition comes before which: the way in which, the reason for which.

60
00:04:32.183 --> 00:04:35.834
Be careful! Don't say: The extent which to it works varies.

61
00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:40.937
Say: The extent to which it works varies.

62
00:04:41.237 --> 00:04:43.225
Put the preposition before 'which'.

63
00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:46.802
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:49.634
Rebuilding Global Institutions.

65
00:04:49.934 --> 00:04:56.822
Most international institutions were designed after 1945, when the world looked very different.

66
00:04:57.833 --> 00:05:02.631
The extent to which they reflect today's emerging powers is one of the biggest reform questions.

67
00:05:03.633 --> 00:05:08.501
The degree to which a reform proposal can win support depends on institutional legitimacy.

68
00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:14.855
Multilateralism works only if the way in which decisions are made seems fair to everyone.

69
00:05:15.867 --> 00:05:22.568
Facing a global challenge such as climate change, collective action and global cooperation are no longer optional.

70
00:05:23.667 --> 00:05:27.552
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:28.417 --> 00:05:31.751
The extent blank institutions are fair is debated.

72
00:05:32.051 --> 00:05:35.403
A, to which. B, which. C, of that.

73
00:05:38.967 --> 00:05:40.815
The answer is A: to which.

74
00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:44.762
The way blank decisions are made affects trust.

75
00:05:45.062 --> 00:05:48.402
A, which in. B, in which. C, that in.

76
00:05:51.967 --> 00:05:53.757
The answer is B: in which.

77
00:05:54.917 --> 00:05:56.614
Choose the correct sentence.

78
00:05:56.914 --> 00:06:05.409
A, The degree to which power is shared matters.. B, The degree which to power is shared matters.. C, The degree to that power is shared matters..

79
00:06:08.967 --> 00:06:12.557
The answer is A: The degree to which power is shared matters..

80
00:06:13.717 --> 00:06:18.003
A state that is gaining economic and political influence is an blank power.

81
00:06:18.303 --> 00:06:21.539
A, fading. B, emerging. C, neutral.

82
00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:27.332
The answer is B: emerging.

83
00:06:28.483 --> 00:06:31.714
According to the reading, when were most institutions designed?

84
00:06:32.014 --> 00:06:38.976
A, after 1945. B, after 2000. C, before 1900.

85
00:06:42.533 --> 00:06:45.717
The answer is A: after 1945.

86
00:06:46.933 --> 00:06:50.236
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:51.083 --> 00:06:55.707
What is one reform you would make to how international institutions operate today?

88
00:07:04.517 --> 00:07:05.854
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:07:06.154 --> 00:07:35.559
One reform I would make is to give emerging powers and smaller regions a fairer voice in key decisions, for example by reforming the Security Council. Institutions gain legitimacy when their structure reflects the present world rather than 1945. A fairer system would improve trust, make collective action easier and encourage countries to follow the rules they helped to write.

90
00:07:35.859 --> 00:07:37.707
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:38.617 --> 00:07:43.916
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and the extent and degree to which plus clause.

92
00:07:44.216 --> 00:07:49.666
Today's value is strategic vision. See the bigger picture, and plan for where you want to be.

93
00:07:49.966 --> 00:07:52.549
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

94
00:07:52.849 --> 00:07:55.989
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

